---
export const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What are anagrams?',
    a: 'Anagrams are words or phrases made by rearranging the letters of another word or phrase, using every letter exactly once. “Listen” and “silent” are anagrams of each other, as are “evil” and “vile”.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is an anagram example?',
    a: 'Classic examples: “listen” = “silent”, “dormitory” = “dirty room”, “the eyes” = “they see”, and “astronomer” = “moon starer”. Each pair uses exactly the same letters in a different order.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are the 7 letter words with anagram?',
    a: 'Many 7-letter words have anagrams. Examples: “present” and “serpent”, “teacher”, “cheater” and “hectare”, and “senator”, “treason” and “atoners”. Use Word Finder mode with your 7 letters to list every word they can make.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the anagram of snake?',
    a: 'The anagram of “snake” is “sneak”. Both words use the letters A, E, K, N and S exactly once.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is an anagram solver?',
    a: 'An anagram solver is a tool that takes a set of letters and finds every word or phrase that can be made from them. This one handles single words and multi-word anagrams, and runs entirely in your browser.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the anagram definition?',
    a: 'The anagram definition is simple: a word or phrase formed by rearranging all the letters of another word or phrase, using each letter exactly once.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is this an anagram maker for names?',
    a: 'Yes. It works as an anagram maker, creator and finder for names, words and sentences. Spaces and punctuation are ignored, so you can paste a full name.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I use it as an anagrams cheat for word games?',
    a: 'Yes. Word Finder mode lists every word you can spell from your letters, which makes it a quick anagrams cheat for Scrabble, Wordle-style puzzles and crosswords.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is an anagram?',
    a: 'An anagram is a word or phrase made by rearranging the letters of another one, using every letter exactly once. “Listen” becomes “silent”, and “dormitory” becomes “dirty room”.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does the anagram generator work?',
    a: 'It counts the letters you enter, finds every dictionary word that fits inside them, then searches for combinations of words that use all the letters exactly once. It runs in a background thread, so the page stays responsive.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why do I get so many odd results?',
    a: 'Long phrases have thousands of valid combinations. Keep Common Words Only on, lower Max Words, or raise Min Word Length to cut the noise. Use Must Include to build around a word you like.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I find anagrams of my name?',
    a: 'Yes. Enter your full name; spaces and punctuation are ignored. Try Must Include with a word you want, such as “love”, for personalized results.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does the Word Finder do?',
    a: 'It lists single words instead of full anagrams: words you can spell using only your letters, or words that contain all of your letters. It is handy for word games.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is my text sent anywhere?',
    a: 'No. The dictionary is downloaded once and every search happens locally. History and favorites are stored only in your browser.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="scroll-mt-20 border-t border-hairline">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-300 px-4 py-24 sm:px-6 md:py-32">
    <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="heading-lg mt-3">Questions, answered.</h2>
    <div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl divide-y divide-hairline border-y border-hairline">
      {
        faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="group py-5">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-sm text-base font-medium text-ink select-none">
              {f.q}
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-mute transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-body">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
  })} />
</section>
